No third-party source code is vendored into this repository. A CI licence gate
(scripts/licence-gate.sh) fails the build on any GPL, AGPL, LGPL or CC BY-NC
licence in the runtime dependency graph. Release artifacts will ship a
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt generated from that graph, plus the vendored assets
below; the release train that attaches it has not landed yet, so no published
artifact carries one today.

One third-party ASSET is vendored, and it is embedded in the binary:

    Inter 4.1 — Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors
    (https://github.com/rsms/inter), licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
    Version 1.1. Vendored at web/src/assets/fonts/ as Inter-Regular-latin.woff2
    (weight 400) and Inter-Medium-latin.woff2 (weight 500). These are MODIFIED
    VERSIONS under the OFL: a Latin subset of the upstream faces, cut by the
    committed, reproducible scripts/subset-fonts.sh. Inter declares no Reserved
    Font Name, so the family name is unchanged. The full licence text is
    committed beside them as web/src/assets/fonts/OFL.txt and reproduced in
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt; the upstream artefact, the subsetting parameters
    and the checksums of both are in web/src/assets/fonts/README.md.

The OFL requires the copyright notice and licence to travel with the font, which
is why they travel with the binary rather than only with the source tree. The
licence gate above cannot see this: it reads the Go module graph, and a font is
not a module. test/repo/web_fonts_test.go is the gate that does.

Dragon Kill Party is a clean-room reimplementation. It contains no source code,
schema text, language strings, or assets from EQdkp Plus, which is licensed
AGPL-3.0 (its game modules and raidlog XSD are CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, non-commercial).
The importer reads a user's own EQdkp Plus database at runtime; that creates no
derivative work.

